# NetMamba+ client edition — packet classifier

**One workflow:** train the native NetMamba+ packet adaptation from the supplied **CICIDS2017 and UNSW CSVs**, then predict benign/attack with the validation-selected **joint pretrained** model. This repo contains the executable code, tests and packet evidence.

Start with [setup and use](SETUP.md), [results and limits](RESULTS.md), or the full [client project explanation](https://github.com/buffbeefalo/netmambaplus-reproduction/blob/main/docs/customer/client-project-guide.md).

The joint model scored **97.56% / 94.29% group-weighted balanced accuracy** on the selected CIC / UNSW test groups. It consumes 1,500 packet bytes and returns two logits, a class and uncalibrated probabilities. This is a packet adaptation: the CSVs cannot establish the original paper's flows, and their packet metrics do not reproduce the paper's 97.50% flow result.

## Check and demonstrate without a GPU

Use Python 3.10 or 3.12 (`python3` if that is your interpreter's name):

```text
git clone https://github.com/buffbeefalo/netmambaplus-client.git
cd netmambaplus-client
python -m unittest discover -s tests -v
python tools/verify_client.py
python tools/render_packet_demo.py --output runs/packet-demo-new
```

Open `runs/packet-demo-new/index.html`. It displays all 25,930 retained joint-model test groups across both sources, including label disagreements. It works offline, including from a client source ZIP. It does not capture traffic, execute new inference or block packets. The verifier recomputes saved packet evidence; optional native tests state their skips.

For actual GPU training and prediction, follow [SETUP.md](SETUP.md). The measured native environment is Linux ARM64 / NVIDIA GB10. Linux, Windows and macOS CI checks the portable software/evidence separately. Other physical GPUs need their own numerical and packet-model checks; native CPU/NPU/SmartNIC execution is not established. [CI results by revision](https://github.com/buffbeefalo/netmambaplus-client/actions/workflows/ci.yml).

## Evidence and updates

All six recorded native comparison models completed 1,000 updates, and all nine controls completed. The UNSW-only metadata control scored 99.34% there, above the neural models. One seed, capped subsets, limited subtype support and unknown prior pretrained exposure constrain the result. Class agreement does not mean bit-identical scores: the original full inference comparison retained two strict logit failures; a later 128-row client check retained 76. [Recorded scopes](https://github.com/buffbeefalo/netmambaplus-reproduction/blob/main/docs/research/client-edition-validation.json).

Development belongs in [netmambaplus-reproduction](https://github.com/buffbeefalo/netmambaplus-reproduction). Verified source exports update this client automatically; manual client divergence stops updates for review. [CLIENT_MANIFEST.json](CLIENT_MANIFEST.json) records the exact source revision and file identities. The full repo explains every component and preserves historical research/teaching materials.

Raw CSVs, upstream source and weights are separate acquisitions. A source clone is not a pretrained application bundle. See [NOTICE.md](NOTICE.md) for attribution and inherited-asset boundaries.
